    "Identity of variance var1, bandwidth bw1, lower correlation Cholesky L and additive noise variance sigma1>1e-5. Omega=L@L.T. The temporal covariance is var1*exp(-bw1*distance^2)+1e-5*I. The flattened PyMC observations y.T.reshape(-1) put category fastest, matching Stan to_vector(y) and temporal_covariance tensor-product Omega. KroneckerNormal sigma=sqrt(sigma1) preserves additive noise variance.",
